{
  "id": "merge-two-level-cards",
  "title": "A card merged twice (L1 -> M -> W) with undos addressed to both losers",
  "covers": [
    "merge: card.merged into a card that is itself merged later (flattening)",
    "replay set: reviews of a loser two levels down count for the final survivor",
    "undo: an undo addressed to a loser's review removes it from the survivor's replay set",
    "undo: earliest undo wins, also for a merged card's review",
    "server verdicts: derived from the device ops by the model's Server (SYNC.md 8.1)"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A has W (食べる, card Wc) and M (持つ, card Mc). B, offline, creates its own L1 for 持つ with card L1c and reviews L1c (r1, T+11).",
    "The server merges L1 into M (seq 6) and, when L1c arrives, L1c into Mc (seq 8): the card was created on a note that is already merged.",
    "A reviews Mc (r2, learning, T+16) and Wc (r3, T+17), then re-matches M to 食べる (T+20). That collides with W: M is merged into W (seq 13) and Mc into Wc (seq 14). L1c.merged_into_id is re-pointed from Mc to Wc (never a chain).",
    "B, still offline, undoes r1 (T+30) and reviews L1c again (r4, T+31). A undoes r2 (T+32); B undoes r2 too, later (T+33): the earliest undo (A's, T+32) is the one recorded.",
    "Wc's replay set is every non-undone schedule-feeding review addressed to Wc, Mc or L1c: r3, r4, in (hlc, id) order. r1 and r2 are undone."
  ],
  "devices": {
